From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toly <1397674+AnatolyRugalev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 18:50:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/62] blitz-traits, blitz-dom: a request carries its
 destination

A NetProvider got a URL and nothing about what it was for, so it could
not decide per kind of resource, as a Content Security Policy does with
img-src, style-src and font-src. Request now has fetch's destination
(Destination: Empty, Document, Iframe, Image, Style, Font), and every
request a document makes says it:

- <img> and CSS images (background-image, mask-image): Image;
- <link rel=stylesheet>, its reload and @import: Style;
- @font-face: Font;
- an <iframe>'s document: Iframe;
- a navigation (NavigationOptions::into_request, blitz's launch): Document.

Request::get leaves it Empty, and Request::destination sets it. The
struct is non_exhaustive already, so the field breaks no one outside.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
